congratulations and welcome to nethack.

[] Pointers are better than complete answers!

okay ...

[] Note: I have so far played only as a barbarian.

seems that many people play as barbarians (even if their character is
a priest or wizard for example) ... sorry about that.

[] 1. What should you #dip your weapon in? I think you drown in pools, so

generally weapon #dip'ping is used in the narrow sense of affecting the
blessed state of the weapon. you can also "poison" arrows (and the like)
by dipping in the right potion. and there's this rumor about the
lady-of-the-lake (Ref. Excalibur) now living in a fountain. btw, it
is possible to "rust-proof" your weapon. the technique was discovered
by a confused player attempting to enhance his weapon.

[] 2. After you #loot a chest, should you put something back in? Is there
[]    any way to get into these chests other than #force? Does #force
[]    have any bad side effects (other than breaking your weapon)?

#loot allows you to take things out of or put things into a chest but
you don't have to do either. chests make good hiding places for things
that you'd rather not have handy monsters find. #force in and of itself
is harmless. small statues may interest you in this matter. lock picks,
or a key that fits are obvious ways of entering a chest. beware, there
are chest traps that can be triggered at odd moments (and there's a
command to deal with it).

[] 3. How do you figure out at which altar you should #offer? I tried
[]    this once and was told that my own lord's power (?) decreased? I
[]    mean how do I know which lord is mine?
[] 4. What does "Chaotic" in my stats mean?

these questions are related. you character has an alignment, the
default for a barbarian is "chaotic". altars have a default alignment,
also. when the current alignment of an altar matches your current
alignment then you've established a direct connection to the god of that
alignment. with _experience_ and a little luck you'll be able to convert
non-aligned altars (use :look to identify them) to your alignment. you
can, of course, change your alignment during play (mostly non-trivial).

monsters also have alignment. the tendency is for co-aligned creatures
not to attack each other. if at all possible grab a copy of the NetHack
guidebook (i've got a pure text version).

[] 5. To feed your dog/cat should you throw food at him, or drop food and
[]    walk away, or throw food next to him? Also when trying to train it
[]    to steal (I believe this is done by rewarding your pet when it
[]    picks some stuff) should you reward it when it picks something up
[]    or when it drops it? Should you feed it and then pick the stuff up,

since food can be found laying around it is significant when you throw
food at a monster and it eats the food. when training a pet you should
immediately (asap) reward the behavior that you want to reinforce. it
is best when you let your pet do all the work ...

[] 6. What good are statues?

you heard about small ones. if you don't dig statues then you can't
appreciate their utility ...

also a preponderence of statues on a given level means something is
creating them! you may not want to look into the possiblity in this
case.

[] 7. What do those messages like "you hear the footsteps of a guard"
[]    mean?

they are often coupled with "you hear someone counting money".
magic mapping will occasionally reveal the presence of a small room
unconnected to the rest of a normal level. the romans had a phrase,
"ad aerarium" meaning "to the gold", ask the oracle. this message
is often used to locate a teleport trap that can send you to the
vault but not always. how you get out of the vault is your business.

[] 8. What monsters can be safely eaten and are there any side effects?

as a barbarian, i believe you are poison resistant, and so you can
eat all fresh kills without problem. no one can eat tainted food
safely (there are cures).

might i suggest that you try other characters. i like wizards, priests,
and healers and these are admittedly harder characters to play initially.
however, they have special abilities/features which are enlightening.
you might also enjoy valkyries and samurais <sp?>.

